  "generated_text": "To solve for \\( g(4) \\), we need to determine the function \\( g \\) and then evaluate it at 4. Let's start by understanding the relationship between \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(f(x)) \\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ f(x) = 2x - 3 \\]\n\\[ g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \\]\n\nWe need to express \\( g \\) in terms of \\( x \\). To do this, let's find the value of \\( x \\) such that \\( f(x) = 4 \\). We set up the equation:\n\\[ f(x) = 4 \\]\n\\[ 2x - 3 = 4 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[ 2x - 3 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 2x = 4 + 3 \\]\n\\[ 2x = 7 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{7}{2} \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( x = \\frac{7}{2} \\) into the expression for \\( g(f(x)) \\) to find \\( g(4) \\):\n\\[ g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \\]\n\\[ g(4) = 5 - 4 \\left( \\frac{7}{2} \\right) \\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[ g(4) = 5 - 4 \\cdot \\frac{7}{2} \\]\n\\[ g(4) = 5 - 2 \\cdot 7 \\]\n\\[ g(4) = 5 - 14 \\]\n\\[ g(4) = -9 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( g(4) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-9}\n\\]",
